---
source: src/adapter/mcp/open_tools.rs
assertion_line: 429
expression: tool.description.clone().unwrap_or_default()
---
Show a running process to the user in a new pane beside yours in the terminal workspace you run in, attached to it, without taking the user's focus. read_only=true opens it watch-only. direction is one of right, down; without it the pane splits along its longer side. Returns {project, process, pane, read_only, alerts}. Outside a terminal workspace: isError, kind no-workspace; the message names the muster attach command to ask the user to run in their own terminal. A process that is not running is not-running: start it first with process_start.
